Upstream

The editor's canvas grid, web/src/editor/table/grid/, is derived from the grid component of
Teable (https://github.com/teableio/teable), packages/sdk/src/components/grid/, Copyright (c)
2023-2025 Teable, Inc., used under the MIT License (below). Most of its files are copies of
Teable's, some unchanged and the rest modified by the Kition authors; the others are the Kition
authors' own. web/src/editor/table/grid/_shim/grid-core.ts stands in for Teable's @teable/core and
carries the select colour list of its packages/core/src/models/field/colors.ts (MIT, same
copyright). The code comes only from Teable's MIT-licensed packages/, not from its AGPL-3.0
applications. docs/attribution.md lists the files.

The rest of the kit has no upstream. Its engine, request layer, import, and editor (with the grid
above) were moved here from Kition (KitionAI/kition, Apache-2.0) at commit
7ee7b5387b6993d370c325261fd4bf806a596143; this repository is their source of truth since.

Third-party material

The engine bundles SQLite (public domain), compiled to WebAssembly through rusqlite and
sqlite-wasm-rs (MIT). The editor bundles the npm packages listed in web/package.json under their
own licenses (MIT, ISC, Apache-2.0). docs/attribution.md lists them, and the repository's assets,
with their sources and licenses.

Icons from Lucide (https://lucide.dev), under the ISC License, with the icons Lucide derives from
Feather under the MIT License (both texts below): the engine's picture renderer links
kition-tessera-icons and the editor bundles @kition/tessera-icons (KitionAI/kition-tessera,
Apache-2.0), whose `lucide:` icons are Lucide 1.55.0 path data; their LICENSE-lucide lists the
Feather-derived ones.

Fonts

The web package ships and embeds no font. The headless
kition-table executable (built with the `embed` feature of crates/view/fonts) builds in three
faces from kition-fonts (https://github.com/KitionAI/kition-fonts): Inter (SIL Open Font License
1.1, Copyright 2020 The Inter Project Authors), Noto Color Emoji (SIL Open Font License 1.1,
Copyright 2022 Google Inc.) and Droid Sans Fallback (Apache-2.0, Copyright (c) 2005-2008 The
Android Open Source Project). The SIL Open Font License text is at the end of this file.

Loro (https://github.com/loro-dev/loro), Copyright (c) 2022 Zixuan Chen, is under the MIT License
(below). The editor bundles it as loro-crdt 1.16.4 (through @kition/kit-editor), and the engine
links its Rust crates (loro 1.16.2, through kition-sdk's Loro dependency in kition-kdm). The MPL-2.0
crates im, sized-chunks and bitmaps listed below come with Loro, in the editor and the engine alike.

MPL-2.0 dependencies

These Rust crates are under the Mozilla Public License 2.0 and are used unmodified; their source
is available from crates.io and the repositories below.

- bitmaps (MPL-2.0 or later): https://github.com/bodil/bitmaps
- im (MPL-2.0 or later): https://github.com/bodil/im-rs
- sized-chunks (MPL-2.0 or later): https://github.com/bodil/sized-chunks

